II. Registration & Team Formation
Q: Is there a registration fee?
A: No. The Hackathon is free to join.
Q: Can I register if I don’t have a team?
A: Yes. Individual Builders can participate independently, join the official TG community to find teammates, or form a team on-site.
Q: Can I still participate if I don’t have time to complete the Hackathon Developer Registration?
A: Yes. You only need to complete the GWDC Hackathon registration: https://luma.com/be2le0l0 ,
and submit your project before the final submission deadline, September 30, 12:00 KST.
Q: What is the maximum team size?
A: Each team can have up to 5 members, including the Team Leader.
Q: Can I participate remotely?
A: Yes, although on-site participation is strongly recommended.
Q: Do team members need to register separately after the Team Leader registers?
A: No. The Team Leader can provide the team and team member information during registration. Please also make sure all team members join the official TG Group to receive subsequent updates.
Q: Are the current Ecosystems and Challenges final?
A: For now, yes:
① 🔸TRON:
https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HXLhu1_vCoMD5aN3APEYEjDrh9oVCj7g/view
② 🔸FuriosaAI x Bricksum:
https://docs.google.com/document/d/13qh7oePGl7Flrl-Zh_A6hfr02L266PvS/edit
Any further updates will be shared in the GWDC TG Group.
Q: Can I participate in multiple Challenges across multiple Ecosystems?
A: Yes. You may submit separately using different email addresses.
Please note: We do not recommend submitting the same or highly similar project multiple times just to improve its ranking.

III. Project Development & Submission
Q: What materials do I need to submit?
A: Please prepare the following:
-Challenge selection
-GitHub / Code Repository
-Project Demo Video, within 3 minutes
-Project Introduction and Pitch Deck
Q: Do I have to build a completely new project from scratch? Can I use existing code?
A:
🔸 TRON: You do not have to start from scratch. You may continue developing an existing project or product prototype, but the submission must include clearly defined new features or substantial improvements specifically related to the Challenge. Existing code can also be used, but you must ensure that you have the legal right to use it. When submitting, please clearly indicate which parts are existing code and which parts were newly developed for the Hackathon.
🔸 FuriosaAI x Bricksum: Basically, we recommend building the project from scratch rather than using existing code. However, there are currently no specific restrictions or limitations on using existing code.
Q: Does the project have to be open source?
A:
🔸 TRON: Open sourcing is not required. However, participating teams must provide necessary demo materials, documentation, and other materials so that the judging team can verify the authenticity and completion of the project.
🔸 FuriosaAI x Bricksum: Open sourcing is not required.
Q: Where can I find the final project submission form?
A: The project submission form will be shared on-site and in the official TG Group after September 28. Please stay tuned for further updates.

IV. Final Competition & Judging
Q: How many projects will be selected as finalists?
A: Each Hackathon Ecosystem Partner will select Top 3 projects from all submissions, regardless of track. The results and related information will be announced through the official TG Group.
Q: When will the Top 3 projects present?
A: The presentations are expected to start at 15:00 KST on September 30. The Top 3 projects will present on the Innovation Stage.
Q: How long does each project presentation last?
A: 5-minute presentation + 3-minute Q&A with the judges.
Q: How will projects be judged?
A: The judging will take into consideration:
-Challenge alignment
-Innovation
-Technical implementation
-Product completeness
-Practical value
-Demo performance
Q: Do I have to stay on-site for the full 48 hours?
A: No. Participants are not required to stay on-site for the entire event. However, if your project advances to the final Demo stage, you must complete the presentation according to the official schedule.
Q: What if I make it to the Final but cannot be on-site that day?
A: Please contact the Hackathon staff as early as possible to confirm whether a remote Demo is possible. The final arrangement will be subject to the GWDC Organizing Committee.

